{
  "info": {
    "name": "fitmess-api — EPICA-02: Catálogo Global de Ejercicios",
    "_postman_id": "e2c0a002-0002-4002-8002-fitmess0epica02",
    "description": "Colección Postman para la EPICA-02 (Catálogo Global de Ejercicios) de fitmess-api.\n\nCubre HU-005 (crear), HU-006 (modificar), HU-007 (inhabilitar) y los listados/detalle del catálogo.\n\n## Cómo usarla\n\n1. Importa también `fitmess-local.postman_environment.json` y selecciónalo.\n2. Levanta la API: `pnpm run start:dev` (por defecto en `http://localhost:3000`, prefijo global `/api`).\n3. Ejecuta la carpeta `00 — Setup / Auth`:\n   - `Registrar entrenador` crea un COACH nuevo (email dinámico) — solo si aún no tienes uno.\n   - `Login` guarda `accessToken` en el entorno; todas las demás peticiones lo usan vía Bearer heredado.\n4. Ejecuta las carpetas en orden con el Collection Runner: cada request encadena las variables (`exerciseId`, `exerciseName`, `inactiveExerciseId`) que necesitan las siguientes.\n\n## Notas de contrato\n\n- Todos los endpoints de `/exercises` exigen JWT y rol COACH o ADMIN (RN-22). Un ATHLETE recibe 403.\n- Las respuestas exitosas vienen envueltas por `ResponseInterceptor`: `{ success, statusCode, data, meta?, message?, timestamp }`.\n- Los errores usan RFC 9457 con `Content-Type: application/problem+json` y campo extra `errorCode`.\n- `DELETE /exercises/:id` es soft-delete (`isActive=false`) y responde `{ data: null, message }` — nunca bloquea por uso en planes (CA-007-1).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Sufijo único por corrida para que los nombres de ejercicio no colisionen",
          "// entre ejecuciones (la unicidad de name es case-insensitive entre activos).",
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('runSuffix')) {",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('runSuffix', String(Date.now()).slice(-6));",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000/api", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "runSuffix", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "exerciseId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "exerciseName", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "inactiveExerciseId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "usedExerciseId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 — Setup / Auth",
      "description": "Obtención del token. Los endpoints de ejercicios requieren rol COACH o ADMIN.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Registrar entrenador (COACH)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Email e identificación dinámicos: ambos son únicos en la plataforma.",
                  "const s = pm.collectionVariables.get('runSuffix');",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('coachEmail', `coach.epica02.${s}@ejemplo.com`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('coachIdNumber', `10${s}000`.slice(0, 10));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Guarda credenciales para el login', () => {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('coachEmail', pm.collectionVariables.get('coachEmail'));",
                  "  pm.environment.set('coachPassword', 'MiClaveSegura123');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Carlos Andres Gomez Ruiz\",\n  \"email\": \"{{coachEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"MiClaveSegura123\",\n  \"phone\": \"3101234567\",\n  \"phoneCountryCode\": \"57\",\n  \"identificationType\": \"CC\",\n  \"identificationNumber\": \"{{coachIdNumber}}\",\n  \"dateOfBirth\": \"1992-05-14\",\n  \"acceptedTerms\": true,\n  \"acceptedDataProcessing\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/coaches/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "coaches", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Crea un entrenador para poder operar el catálogo. Si ya tienes un COACH o ADMIN registrado, salta este request y usa directamente `Login` con tus credenciales.\n\nEl cuerpo puede requerir ajustes según los campos exactos de `RegisterCoachDto` (consentimientos legales — Ley 1581/2012)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (guarda accessToken)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const data = body.data ?? body;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve accessToken', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(data).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessToken', data.accessToken);",
                  "if (data.refreshToken) pm.environment.set('refreshToken', data.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{coachEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{coachPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Autentica y guarda `accessToken` en el entorno. El resto de la colección lo hereda como Bearer token.\n\nEste endpoint está bajo rate limiting (`@nestjs/throttler`): un exceso de intentos responde 429."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "HU-005 — Crear ejercicio",
      "description": "POST /exercises. Crea `Exercise` + primera `ExerciseVersion` (versionNumber = 1) en una sola `$transaction` (CA-005-1). `isActive` queda en true. Visible de inmediato, sin aprobación (CA-005-3).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Crear ejercicio — 201 (happy path)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const s = pm.collectionVariables.get('runSuffix');",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('exerciseName', `Sentadilla con barra ${s}`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Envelope estandar del ResponseInterceptor', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('success', true);",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('statusCode', 201);",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('timestamp');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const ex = body.data;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Primera version: versionNumber = 1 (CA-005-1)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(ex.versionNumber).to.eql(1);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Nace activo, sin paso de aprobacion (CA-005-3)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(ex.isActive).to.eql(true);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('No expone campos internos', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(ex).to.not.have.property('archivedAt');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('exerciseId', ex.id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('exerciseId', ex.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"{{exerciseName}}\",\n  \"description\": \"Parado con los pies al ancho de los hombros, descender flexionando cadera y rodillas manteniendo la espalda neutra, hasta que los muslos queden paralelos al piso.\",\n  \"muscleGroup\": \"Cuadriceps\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"]
            },
            "description": "Crea el ejercicio y guarda su `id` en `exerciseId` para el resto de la colección.\n\n**Campos** (decisión del 2026-08-05 — sin equipo, dificultad ni multimedia):\n- `name` (2–150): identidad del catálogo, vive en `Exercise`, **no se versiona**.\n- `description` (1–1000): contenido de entrenamiento, vive en `ExerciseVersion`.\n- `muscleGroup` (1–50): texto libre, sin enum en esta épica."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Crear duplicado — 409 DUPLICATE_ENTITY (CA-005-2)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Content-Type problem+json (RFC 9457)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/problem+json');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('errorCode DUPLICATE_ENTITY', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().errorCode).to.eql('DUPLICATE_ENTITY');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"  {{exerciseName}}  \",\n  \"description\": \"Variante enviada con el mismo nombre en mayusculas y con espacios sobrantes.\",\n  \"muscleGroup\": \"Cuadriceps\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"]
            },
            "description": "Reenvía el mismo `name` del request anterior, con espacios sobrantes, para demostrar que la unicidad es **case-insensitive y con trim** entre ejercicios **activos** (CA-005-2).\n\nRequiere haber ejecutado antes `Crear ejercicio — 201`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Crear sin campos obligatorios — 400",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Content-Type problem+json', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/problem+json');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Detalla los errores de validacion', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('errorCode');",
                  "  pm.expect(JSON.stringify(body)).to.include('nombre');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"A\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"muscleGroup\": \"\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"]
            },
            "description": "`name` de 1 carácter (mínimo 2), `description` y `muscleGroup` vacíos. El `ValidationPipe` global rechaza con 400 y mensajes en español."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Crear sin token — 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Ejercicio sin autenticar\",\n  \"description\": \"Este request no lleva Authorization header.\",\n  \"muscleGroup\": \"Pectoral\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"]
            },
            "description": "Sin `Authorization`. El `JwtAuthGuard` rechaza antes de llegar al controller."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "HU-005 / HU-007 — Listar catálogo",
      "description": "GET /exercises. Lista paginada con la versión vigente embebida. Por defecto solo activos (CA-007-2).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Listar catálogo — 200 (defaults)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Trae meta de paginacion', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.meta).to.have.all.keys(",
                  "    'page', 'limit', 'totalItems', 'totalPages', 'hasNext', 'hasPrevious'",
                  "  );",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Defaults page=1 limit=20', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.meta.page).to.eql(1);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.meta.limit).to.eql(20);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Solo ejercicios activos por defecto (CA-007-2)', () => {",
                  "  body.data.forEach((e) => pm.expect(e.isActive).to.eql(true));",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Cada fila embebe su version vigente', () => {",
                  "  if (body.data.length) {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data[0]).to.have.property('versionNumber');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data[0]).to.have.property('muscleGroup');",
                  "  }",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"]
            },
            "description": "Sin query params: `page=1`, `limit=20`, `includeInactive=false`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Listar paginado — 200 (page & limit)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const meta = pm.response.json().meta;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Respeta los query params', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(meta.page).to.eql(1);",
                  "  pm.expect(meta.limit).to.eql(5);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('No devuelve mas items que el limit', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.length).to.be.at.most(5);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises?page=1&limit=5",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "1", "description": "Número de página (base 1)" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "5", "description": "Resultados por página (máx. 100)" }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Listar incluyendo inhabilitados — 200 (includeInactive)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Puede incluir filas con isActive=false', () => {",
                  "  const data = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "  pm.expect(data).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  data.forEach((e) => pm.expect(e).to.have.property('isActive'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises?includeInactive=true&limit=50",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "includeInactive", "value": "true", "description": "Incluye los inhabilitados (default false)" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "50", "description": "Resultados por página (máx. 100)" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Única vía para auditar el catálogo completo — esta épica no define reactivación.\n\nCon `includeInactive=true` el listado **puede mostrar dos filas con el mismo `name`** (una activa y una inhabilitada): consecuencia aceptada de CA-005-6. El campo `isActive` de cada fila permite distinguirlas.\n\nEl parser del query param usa `@Transform` explícito porque `Boolean('false') === true` en JavaScript."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Listar con limit fuera de rango — 400",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Mensaje sobre el limite maximo', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(JSON.stringify(pm.response.json())).to.include('limite');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises?page=0&limit=500",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "0", "description": "Inválido: la página mínima es 1" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "500", "description": "Inválido: el límite máximo es 100" }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Listar sin token — 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises"]
            },
            "description": "El catálogo no es público: ni el listado ni el detalle son accesibles para un ATHLETE (RN-22). Su acceso vía planes es contenido de EPICA-03."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "HU-006 / HU-007 — Detalle con historial",
      "description": "GET /exercises/:id. Datos vigentes + historial completo de versiones (CA-006-2). No filtra por `isActive` (CA-007-3).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Detalle de ejercicio — 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const ex = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Incluye el historial de versiones (CA-006-2)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(ex.versions).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(ex.versions[0]).to.have.property('versionNumber');",
                  "  pm.expect(ex.versions[0]).to.have.property('createdAt');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('El id coincide con el solicitado', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(ex.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('exerciseId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/exercises/{{exerciseId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["exercises", "{{exerciseId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Devuelve los datos vigentes (los de la versión con mayor `versionNumber`) más el historial completo: `versionNumber` + `createdAt` de cada versión.\n\nNo filtra por `isActive` — un ejercicio inhabilitado se lee igual, con su estado visible, para que un plan histórico pueda mostrarlo indicando que ya no está activo (CA-007-3)."
          }
        },
